  "title": "Euclid parameters always generate a primitive triple",
  "status": "PARTIAL",
  "source_file": "runs/orchestrator/20260823-182407-565694/project_plan.json",
  "statement": "For all positive integers m and n with m > n, gcd(m,n) = 1, and m and n of opposite parity, if a = m^2 - n^2, b = 2mn, and c = m^2 + n^2, then a, b, c are positive integers satisfying a^2 + b^2 = c^2 and gcd(a,b,c) = 1.",
